pub const fn funnel_shl(self, right: usize, n: u32) -> usize

🔬This is a nightly-only experimental API. (funnel_shifts #145686)

Performs a left funnel shift.

This operation can be thought of as concatenating self and right into an integer twice the size of usize, performing a left shift by n, and returning the left half of the result.

The name comes from “funneling” a wider integer to a narrower integer.

§Panics

This function will panic if n is greater than or equal to the number of bits in self.

§Examples

    #![feature(funnel_shifts)]

    let a = 0x0aa00000000006e1_usize;
    let b = 0x2fe78e45983acd98_usize;

    assert_eq!(a.funnel_shl(b, 12), 0x00000000006e12fe);

    // Using zeros as the right operand acts as a normal shift left
    assert_eq!(a.funnel_shl(0, 12), a << 12);

    // Shifting by 0 returns `self` unchanged
    assert_eq!(a.funnel_shl(b, 0), a);

    // Using the same value as the right operand acts as a rotate
    assert_eq!(a.funnel_shl(a, 12), a.rotate_left(12));

Note that while funnel_shl can act as a rotate, it does not allow for rotating by an unbounded amount like rotate_left does:

ⓘ

    #![feature(funnel_shifts)]

    let a = usize::MAX;
    // Okay
    let _ = a.rotate_left(usize::BITS);
    // Panics
    let _ = a.funnel_shl(a, usize::BITS);

Source

